 not mean you own it.</p></article><article><span>02 / CONFIRMED BEFORE FORMING</span><h2>Use the completed month.</h2><p>The last completed month sets the confirmed accumulation zone. The current month is forming and may change. If the assessment supports buying and confirmed Pace is P2, the display reads “Buy gradually · P2”.</p></article><article><span>03 / RISK BEFORE SPEED</span><h2>P4 is never a shortcut.</h2><p>P4 is not a company-quality rating. It describes accelerated buying conditions relative to price history. A lower share price alone cannot make a weak business a Buy. Business risks can still require Reduce, Sell or Avoid. P0 pauses additions; it is not a sell signal or a return forecast.</p></article><article><span>04 / MAKE IT YOURS</span><h2>Start with a sensible budget.</h2><p>Pace zones do not prescribe an automatic purchase amount. Keep the total within your cash budget, concentration limits and risk tolerance. Missing price history leaves business research available without inventing a Pace level.</p></article></section><section class="education-method"><h2>Clear rules. Visible limits.</h2><p>AURYN uses disclosed research heuristics. It does not guarantee returns or replace your judgment. Review the business, valuation assumptions and portfolio fit before acting.</p><a href="/methodology">Read the methodology →</a></section><footer><a href="/">AURYN</a><a href="/about">About</a><a href="/contact">Contact</a><a href="mailto:support@auryninvest.com">support@auryninvest.com</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a></footer></main>'
  
